alue "2005798"} "Doubles, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2005839"} "Doubles, Mixed"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "900321"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "90016742"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "42000"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "42214"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "42470"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "42726"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "257994"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "304000"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "351550"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19005200"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/123"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Singles, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 July –  5 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2159"} "Porte de la Chapelle Arena, Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2005600"} "41 from 36 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In the group stages, there were two seeds eliminated. " [:a {:href "/athletes/2103599"} "Anthony Sinisuka Ginting"] " (INA), bronze medalist from 2020, was defeated by the host nation’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/150930"} "Toma Junior Popov"] ", in a close match lasting well over an hour by 21-19, 17-21, 21-15. The other seed to be eliminated was " [:a {:href "/athletes/143712"} "Jonatan Christie"] " (INA), who lost to " [:a {:href "/athletes/2503208"} "Lakshya Sen"] " (IND) by a score of 21-18, 21-12. All the other groups were won by the-seeded players – besides Popov, the only players to advance not from Asian nations were Denmark’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/133435"} "Viktor Axelsen"] ", the 2020 victor in this event, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/142158"} "Anders Antonsen"] ", world ranked second and third."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Three of the top four seeds had a bye into the quarter-finals. The highlight of the round of 16 was the victory of 2023 World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504061"} "Kunlavut Vitidsarn"] " (THA) over " [:a {:href "/athletes/150945"} "Kenta Nishimoto"] " (JPN) by 16-21, 21-14, 21-12 in a match lasting 80 minutes. The remaining matches in this round went to form in the top half of the draw, " [:a {:href "/athletes/145203"} "Lee Zii Jia"] " (MAS) defeating the unseeded Popov by two games to nil. However, in the bottom half of the draw, the lower ranked players all won, " [:a {:href "/athletes/136076"} "Chou Tien-Chen"] " (TPE) defeating " [:a {:href "/athletes/2503373"} "Kodai Naraoka"] " (JPN) by 21-12, 21-16, unseeded " [:a {:href "/athletes/2503208"} "Lakshya Sen"] " (IND) defeating his countryman " [:a {:href "/athletes/1303425"} "H. S. Sunil Kumar"] " 21-12, 21-6, and finally " [:a {:href "/athletes/146533"} "Loh Kean Yew"] " (SGP) winning by 23-21, 21-15 against higher ranked " [:a {:href "/athletes/2502744"} "Li Shifeng"] " (CHN), winner of the Boy’s Singles at the 2018 Youth Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the quarter-finals, the lower-seeded players continued their success in the top half of the draw. The top seed " [:a {:href "/athletes/2103168"} "Shi Yuqi"] " (CHN) lost to the lower-seeded Kunlavut Vitidsarn 21-12, 21-10. Lee Zii Jia then defeated the Dane Anders Antonsen 21-17, 21-15. In the lower half of the draw, a close encounter saw Lakshya Sen overcome Chou Tien-Chen 19-21, 21-15, 21-12, in the only quarter-final to go to three games. Viktor Axelsen completed the semi-final line-up with a comfortable victory over Loh Kean Yew by 21-9, 21-17."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With no Chinese players in the semi-finals, Viktor Axelsen saw an opportunity to defend his title, and defeated Sen by 22-20, 21-14. His opponent in the final was to be Vitidsarn, who defeated Lee in the other semi-final by 21-14, 21-15."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the match for the bronze medal, after an uncertain start it was Lee who defeated Sen by 13-21, 21-16, 21-11. In the final, Vitidsarn tried his best but was outclassed by a dominant Axelsen, who won 21-11, 21-11, so retaining his Olympic crown."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133435"} "Viktor Axelsen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2504061"} "Kunlavut Vitidsarn"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/THA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/THA.png"}] "THA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/145203"} "Lee Zii Jia"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MAS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MAS.png"}] "MAS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2503208"} "Lakshya Sen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IND"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IND.png"}] "IND"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :sty